  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math>&nbsp;be the foot of perpendicular drawn from the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;to the plane <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>14</mn></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;is a point on the plane such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>, then the area of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi></math> is equal to</p><p>Now plotting the diagram of given value we get,</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0166_ed47a6f301d5.png\" style=\"width: 280px; height: 180px;\" /></p><p>Now given plane&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>14</mn></math></p><p>Length of perpendicular from&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>to</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Q</mi></math>&nbsp;will be</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>14</mn></mrow><msqrt><mn>6</mn></msqrt></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>6</mn></msqrt></math></p><p>Now in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#9651;</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>cot</mi><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math></p><p>So,&nbsp; Area of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><msqrt><mn>6</mn></msqrt><mo>&#215;</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
